Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:04:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ask every click which block it is for

The pillar aimed at the block in its feet and put the button down in the same breath, which made it the last click in the mod that did. Every other one - a block to break in the way, a face to place against, a door, a chest, a crop - is asked for with the crosshair already on the block or with the hand arrived at the point it was sent to, and the button is pressed a beat later by the helper, by which time the question has been answered or not. When the crosshair is somewhere else by the time that beat runs out, the click lands there instead: for the pillar, a block broken beside the one it meant, or with a throwaway in hand a block placed against the wall.

The pillar now asks the question Movement#prepared and the door branch of MovementTraverse ask, and keeps the old blind click as the fallback for a block with no face to aim at (the shape is empty, so there is no point to reach), so nothing that used to break stalls now.

ClickGatesTest counts it, the way CameraWritesTest, HandWritesTest and ButtonWritesTest count the camera, the hand and the button. It scans the movement and process layers for every click - twenty four of them, pinned per file - and asserts each is behind one of the questions the mod actually asks: the ray on the block, the hand arrived at its point, a place attempt that has confirmed the face, the block under the crosshair a process picked out, or breaking out of a wall the body is inside. A click with none of them carries the sentence "ungated click:" with its reason, which is what the two old ones do - the blind break Movement#prepared falls back to, and the bucket taken out of the water the player is standing in. The count has teeth: the pillar's click put back the way it was fails it with the file and the line.
